// ============================================================================
// HerbChain redesigned schema — BASE
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// This folder (prisma/schema/*.prisma) is the TARGET database architecture for
// the redesigned HerbChain backend. It is NOT yet wired into package.json /
// the running app — the active schema remains prisma/schema.prisma until the
// migration step flips package.json's `prisma.schema` to this folder.
//
// Domain layout (files are ordered by dependency, models may reference each
// other across files):
//   00_base.prisma          generator + datasource + conventions
//   01_identity.prisma      users + addresses (login/identity core)
//   02_security.prisma      sessions, api keys, global audit log
//   03_assets.prisma        files/media + polymorphic entity attachments
//   10_catalogue.prisma     AYUSH species taxonomy + localized content
//   20_agronomy.prisma      farmer profile, plots, crop plans, farm activity
//   30_logistics.prisma     transporter/manufacturer profiles, warehouses,
//                           stock movements
//   40_quality.prisma       lab profile, structured test parameters/results
//   50_trace.prisma         batches (the traceable lots) + append-only events
//   60_products.prisma      finished products + batch composition
//   70_commerce.prisma      purchase orders, invoices, payments, wallets
//   80_compliance.prisma    licenses, inspections, recalls, support tickets
//   90_notifications.prisma templates, notifications, device tokens
//   95_intel.prisma         price quotes, weather snapshots
//   97_blockchain.prisma    blockchain proof anchors
//
// The full conventions reference lives in docs/database/architecture.md.
// ============================================================================

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "sqlite"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Schema-wide conventions (implemented across every file below)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Primary keys: every table gets `id String @id @default(cuid())`.
//    Human-facing identifiers (batch codes, order numbers, invoice numbers,
//    SKUs, license numbers) are separate UNIQUE columns — business keys are
//    never PKs, so they stay renameable/regenerable.
//
// 2. Timestamps: `created_at` on everything, `updated_at` on mutable rows.
//    Trace records (BatchEvent, StockMovement, AuditLog, Payment) are
//    append-only and deliberately have NO `updated_at`.
//
// 3. Soft delete: `deleted_at` ONLY on mutable master data where a hard
//    delete would destroy history (User, Species, Product). Supply-chain
//    records are immutable by design.
//
// 4. Enums: SQLite has no native enums in Prisma, so enumerable columns are
//    TEXT with code-level validation (zod + a single constants module). The
//    allowed values are listed in a comment above every such column.
//
// 5. Money: stored as INTEGER minor units (`*_paise`) — never Float.
//    Serializers convert to decimal rupees for the wire format.
//    Int ceiling = ~21.4M INR per column; documented in architecture.md.
//
// 6. Dates: stored as DateTime (UTC); "YYYY-MM-DD"-style business dates are
//    formatted at the serializer layer.
//
// 7. Foreign keys reference `id` columns; named relations carry explicit
//    @relation names when a model has multiple FKs to the same target.
//
// 8. `deleted_at`/soft-delete lookups must add the filter in code — Prisma
//    has no row-level default scoping.
// ===========================================================================
